@page "/components/qr-code"

<PageTitle>QR Code — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">QR Code</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    Generate QR codes from any string — URLs, vCards, Wi-Fi — via <a href="https://github.com/davidshimjs/qrcodejs" class="underline">qrcodejs</a>. Static SSR renders an empty <code>div</code>; a <code>up.compiler</code> fills it with <code>new QRCode(el, {...})</code> on every fragment swap.
</p>
<p class="doc-note">Interface follows <a href="https://lumeo.nativ.sh/components/qr-code" class="underline">lumeo.nativ.sh/components/qr-code</a>. Rendered as canvas/table (qrcodejs), no SVG dependency, MIT.</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="QrCodeBasic.razor"><QrCodeBasic /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Dynamic Value</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The QR follows the text box. There is no client state, so the field is real and
    <code>up-autosubmit</code> does the wiring — typing submits, the server re-renders with the
    value in the query string, and the QR is born with it.
</p>
<Example Source="QrCodeDynamic.razor"><QrCodeDynamic /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Error Correction Levels</h2>
<p class="doc-note">Low ~7%, Medium ~15%, Quartile ~25%, High ~30%. Higher is denser but more fault-tolerant.</p>
<Example Source="QrCodeLevels.razor"><QrCodeLevels /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Custom Colors</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Colors default to the theme — foreground modules on a card background — and re-resolve when
    the theme changes. Explicit colors win; <code>ForegroundColor="#ffffff"</code> on a
    <code>bg-primary</code> card is white on the primary surface.
</p>
<Example Source="QrCodeColors.razor"><QrCodeColors /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Without Margin (no quiet zone)</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The quiet zone is the empty border scanners need around the modules. <code>ShowMargin="false"</code>
    drops it, for a QR that sits flush — trade the quiet zone for space when the code is
    decorative, not scanned.
</p>
<Example Source="QrCodeMargin.razor"><QrCodeMargin /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Custom Aria Label</h2>
<p class="doc-note">Screen readers announce the friendly label instead of the raw URL.</p>
